      "resolver_card_text": "Problem: Issue #6 - QSPI locks up at STM32F746G-DISCO board\nContext: repo=STM32CubeF7, labels=bug, internal bug tracker, hal, issue_state=closed\nResolver signal: resolution_status=candidate_fix, confidence=medium, score=0.8\nAssessment: Potential fix identified, but integration status is uncertain.\nCandidate PRs: Fix the bug that HAL_NAND_Read_Page_8b and HAL_NAND_Read_SpareArea_8b cannot read data normally.\nCommit evidence: Fix the bug that HAL_NAND_Read_Page_8b and HAL_NAND_Read_SpareArea_8b cannot read data normally. | [projects][UART] Add missing syscalls.\nPR #103 description: This PR fixed the issue https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/stm32f7xx_hal_driver/issues/6 .\r\n\r\nBy changing the `*buff = *(uint8_t *)deviceaddress;` to `*buff = *(__IO uint8_t *)deviceaddress;` , now the data could be read correctly.\nConstraints: Validate against exact MCU series, board, firmware package version, and local project config before applying.",
